# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. custom-image/apply-patches.sh runs INSIDE a
# Linux container: with CRLF the kernel reads the shebang as "/bin/sh\r", which does
# not exist, and `docker compose build api` dies with a bare "not found" (exit 127).
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows checkouts reintroduces this on every clone, and CI
# (Linux) never reproduces it -- so pin the endings here rather than per-machine.
*.sh text eol=lf
